WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.503
-I'm also very excited about
the Stanley Cup semifinals.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.238
They're in full swing right now.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.340
Three teams remaining --
The Montreal Canadiens,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.210
the Tampa Bay Lightning,
and the New York Islanders!

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.779
-Whoa.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.047
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:15.715
Now as you know, after the game,

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.550
they give out awards like
Most Valuable Player,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.186
but they also give out awards
before the game.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.587
You know that?
-No, I did not know that.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:22.755
-Yeah, I'll show you
what I mean.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.190
It's time for
"Tonight Show Superlatives."

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.591
Here we go.
-Oh.

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:30.963
-♪ Tonight Show Superlatives ♪

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:32.765 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:36.669
-Our first player is from
the Islanders, Ilya Sorokin.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.639 line:0%
Yeah, he was voted "most likely
to kiss with his eyes open."

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:42.008 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.477 line:0%
-[ Smooching ]

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:50.650 line:0%
-Next up from the Lightning
is Erik Cernak.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:54.921 line:0%
He was voted "most likely to be
Bart Simpson's DUI mugshot."

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.323 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.094 line:0%
Next up from the Lightning
is Victor Hedman.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:02.862 line:0%
-Oh, yeah.
-He was voted "most likely

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.597 line:0%
to have just caused an 18-car
pile up with his mind."

00:01:05.597 --> 00:01:07.900 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.070 line:0%
-[ Imitates crash ]

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.741 line:0%
-Next up from the Islanders
is Cory Schneider.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.309 line:0%
He was voted "most likely
to be the love child

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:19.645 line:0%
of Blake Shelton and Barb
from 'Stranger Things.'"

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:21.414 line:0%
-I didn't know
that was an award.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.115 line:0%
-What episode was that?

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:25.384 line:0%
-A very specific award
to give out.

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:26.618 line:0%
-It's rare. It's rare.
-Yeah.

00:01:26.618 --> 00:01:27.787 line:0%
-If that's what you mean.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.657 line:0%
Next, from Montreal,
is Jon Merrill.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:32.792 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.028 line:0%
He was voted "most likely to
push you down a water slide."

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:37.463 line:0%
It's like, "Alright, 3, 2 --

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:39.532 line:0%
Go get 'em, man!"

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.333 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:43.102 line:0%
"You should have seen
your face, man!"

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.570 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:48.074 line:0%
Next up from Montreal
is Michael Frolik.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.042 line:0%
He was voted
"best mustache beard."

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:53.012 line:0%
What does that mean?
Oh, there you go. Hey, not bad.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.613 line:0%
That's pretty cool.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:57.082 line:0%
-That's cool, I like that.

00:01:57.082 --> 00:02:01.521 line:0%
Next up from the Islanders
is Simon Holmstrom.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.255 line:0%
He was voted "most likely
to have the nickname

00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:04.923 line:0%
'Swedish Larry Bird.'"

00:02:04.923 --> 00:02:08.294 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.296 line:0%
[ Swedish accent ] "Yeah,
I throw the three-pointer."

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.530 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.199 line:0%
-[ Normal voice ]
Next up from the Lightning

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.800 line:0%
is Anthony Cirelli.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.069 line:0%
He was voted "most likely

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.570 line:0%
to turn in sharp 90-degree
angles when he walks."

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.875 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:25.644 --> 00:02:28.948 line:0%
[ Snare drum playing ]

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.717 line:0%
And finally, from Montreal,
is Shea Weber.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:33.553 line:0%
He was voted "most likely
to sit down in a restaurant

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.421 line:0%
and just tell the waiter,
'meat.'"

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.123 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.892 line:0%
Those you are your Stanley Cup
semifinal superlatives.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:40.927 line:0%
Go, Islanders!

